hadiths[5]{hadithnumber,text}:
"453","Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya Abu Muhammad and Ahmad ibn Amr ibn al-Sarh, in the same meaning, both saying: Sufyan narrated to us, from Amr, from Yahya ibn Ja'dah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought a writing on a shoulder blade, and he said: Sufficient misguidance for a people is that they seek a book other than their Book, to a prophet other than their Prophet. Then Allah, Mighty and Majestic, revealed: Is it not sufficient for them that We sent down to you the Book which is recited to them."
"454","Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Abu Qilabah, that Umar passed by some Jews and heard them mentioning a supplication from the Torah, so he copied it, then brought it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and began to read it, while the face of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) began to change. A man said: O Ibn al-Khattab, do you not see what is on the face of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? So Umar laid down the book, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, sent me as the Seal, and I have been given comprehensive speech and its seals, and speech has been made concise for me, so let not the confused ones distract you. I said to Abu Qilabah: What are the confused ones? He said: The bewildered."
"455","Ubaydullah ibn Mu'adh narrated to us, al-Mu'tamir narrated to us, from his father, from Abu al-Ala, that the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), his hadith would abrogate one another just as the Quran abrogates one another."
"456","Abdullah ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Abu Khalid, from Ibn Ajlan, from Tawus, from Mu'adh, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not hasten tribulation before it descends, for if you do not do so, the Muslims will not lack among them one who, when he speaks, is guided aright or granted success; but if you hasten, paths will branch out with you here and here and here."
"457","Rawh ibn Ubadah narrated to us, Usamah ibn Zayd, meaning al-Laythi, narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, and he mentioned something similar in meaning."
